Cell["\<\
25% over budget is a mathematical proof, not a judgement call: no genuine \
quantum pair of pentagons can produce that number, so a device reporting it \
is certifiably not what it claims to be. But the catch is the same one Stage \
4 already found for a single copy: an intensity emulator tuned to the exact \
quantum fraction, p = 1/\[Sqrt]5, reproduces this test number-for-number \
\[LongDash] its worst pentad also saturates at 1, not past it \[LongDash] and \
the verdict comes back QUANTUM-CERTIFIED. Catching that particular fake needs \
the geometric lens, not another probability sum; that is the entire reason \
the instrument carries two lenses rather than one.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f7762e9-b1f8-452a-9a67-264a23096994"],

Cell["\<\
There is a known general theorem, though: for large enough cycles \[LongDash] \
nine-sided or larger \[LongDash] combining independent copies this way never \
creates a bigger advantage, and the effect stays dormant. The research maps \
where composition does and does not wake it, across several concrete \
structures \[LongDash] pentagon and heptagon products, the four-pentagon \
Quad-C5 graph, the nonagon join that Stage 11 switches on, and a Paley-graph \
case that is still open:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0fc687b0-70a8-ac41-a9b6-870359faee69"],

Cell["\<\
The composition variants studied \[LongDash] which structures wake the \
effect, and which stay dormant:\
\>", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"308ed2e8-e24a-d747-bda6-a4a713c5c4fa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Module[{green = RGBColor[0.24, 0.55, 0.36], amber = RGBColor[0.80, 0.50, 0.18],
   gray = GrayLevel[0.55], navy = RGBColor[0.16, 0.28, 0.46], ink = \
GrayLevel[0.18], badge, rowBg},
 badge[label_, c_] := Framed[Style[label, 10, White, FontFamily -> \
\"Helvetica\", Bold],
    Background -> c, RoundingRadius -> 10, FrameStyle -> None,
    FrameMargins -> {{9, 9}, {3, 3}}];
 rowBg = Join[{navy}, Table[If[OddQ[i], White, GrayLevel[0.965]], {i, 1, \
6}]];
 Grid[{
   {Style[\"structure\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"],
    Style[\"construction\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"],
    Style[\"result\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"],
    Style[\"verdict\", White, Bold, 11, FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\"]},
   {\"C5\[CircleTimes]C5\", \"two pentagon copies (co-normal)\",
    Row[{\"\[Omega] = 5 \[RightArrow] reaches \", Sqrt[5]}], \
badge[\"ACTIVATES\", green]},
   {\"C7\[CircleTimes]C7\[CircleTimes]C5\", \"two heptagon copies + one \
pentagon (co-normal)\",
    Row[{\"9-clique, load 9\", Sqrt[5], \"/20 \[TildeEqual] 1.006 > 1\"}], \
badge[\"ACTIVATES (mix)\", green]},
   {\"Quad-C5\", \"four-pentagon graph (arXiv:2605.12828)\",
    \"\[Theta] = 3.468,  \[CapitalDelta] = 0.468\", badge[\"ACTIVATES\", \
green]},
   {\"C9\[Vee]C9\[Vee]C9\[Vee]C5\", \"three nonagons + one pentagon \
(co-normal)\",
    \"clique \[GreaterEqual] 17 = 2\:2074+1  (Stage 11)\", badge[\"ACTIVATES \
(catalysis)\", green]},
   {\"Paley(13)\[Vee]3\", \"Paley-13, co-normal cube (3 copies)\",
    \"\[Omega] bracketed in [39, 46]\", badge[\"OPEN\", amber]},
   {\"C9\[CircleTimes]C9\", \"nonagon copies alone\",
    \"never exceed the bound\", badge[\"DORMANT\", gray]}
   },
  Background -> {None, rowBg},
  Frame -> None,
  Dividers -> {None, {2 -> Directive[GrayLevel[0.8], Thin]}},
  Alignment -> {{Left, Left, Left, Center}, Center},
  ItemStyle -> Directive[FontFamily -> \"Helvetica\", 11, ink],
  Spacings -> {2, 1.6},
  ItemSize -> {Automatic, 1.7},
  ImageSize -> 680
  ]
]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[797]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6fb99dc3-0be2-411a-b18d-ca417e914475"],

