Cell["\<\
cct_mbqc_hawking_certification.wl (built earlier in this project on this \
exact mesh) designates the adjacent pair {3k+2, 3k+3} the Hawking mode \
(exterior, the tip) and partner mode (interior); at k=0 that is qubits 2 and \
3. Z-measuring every other qubit to a fixed outcome deletes it from the graph \
(Hein et al., PRA 69, 062311 (2004)) and leaves {2,3} disconnected from the \
rest of the mesh \[LongDash] a Bell pair up to one local Hadamard:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29d78e97-d4cc-4479-842e-e091b8557671"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
I2 = IdentityMatrix[2];
PX = {{0, 1}, {1, 0}}; PZ = {{1, 0}, {0, -1}}; PY = {{0, -I}, {I, 0}};
projPlus[op_] := (I2 + op)/2; projMinus[op_] := (I2 - op)/2;

(* cct_mbqc_hawking_certification.wl designates {3k+2,3k+3} the \
Hawking/partner pair; k=0 -> qubits {2,3} *)
measuredA = Complement[Range[nQ], {2, 3}];
forceGatesA = Table[QuantumOperator[projPlus[PZ], {q}], {q, measuredA}];
circA = QuantumCircuitOperator[Join[gsGates, forceGatesA]];
stA = circA[QuantumState[\"Register\", ConstantArray[2, nQ]]];
ampsA = Normal[stA[\"Amplitudes\"]];
nzA = Select[ampsA, Chop[#[[2]]] =!= 0 &];
psi23 = Table[SelectFirst[nzA, #[[1, 1]][[2 ;; 3]] == bits &][[2]], {bits, \
{{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}}}];
psi23 = psi23/Norm[psi23]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[803]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b1ad99a4-e30c-42f2-aff9-738dfcb85143"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[803]=",ExpressionUUID->"75ac7ffc-cbd6-488d-8d79-26587138955b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
That is exactly (|00\:27e9+|01\:27e9+|10\:27e9-|11\:27e9)/2 = \
(H\[CircleTimes]I)|\[CapitalPhi]\:207a\:27e9. The geometric lens (Stage 5) \
prices entanglement by exactly this correlation-matrix construction; turned \
on the carved pair it reads the Tsirelson-optimal violation off the exact \
singular values, not a sampled estimate:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3aa24bf9-63de-4677-8d4d-12de22c9163a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
paulis = {PX, PY, PZ};
Tmat = FullSimplify[Table[Conjugate[psi23] . (KroneckerProduct[paulis[[i]], \
paulis[[j]]] . psi23), {i, 1, 3}, {j, 1, 3}]];
sv = SingularValueList[Tmat];
Smax = FullSimplify[2 Sqrt[sv[[1]]^2 + sv[[2]]^2]];
CFval = FullSimplify[(Smax - 2)/2];
Grid[{
   {Style[\"correlation matrix T\", Bold], MatrixForm[Tmat]},
   {Style[\"singular values\", Bold], sv},
   {Style[\"CHSH optimum S\", Bold], Row[{Smax, \"  \[TildeEqual]  \", \
N[Smax]}]},
   {Style[\"contextual fraction CF\", Bold], Row[{CFval, \"  \[TildeEqual]  \
\", N[CFval]}]}
  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left, Spacings -> {1.3, 1.1}, Background -> \
{None, {GrayLevel[0.93]}}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[804]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7aec0352-15e4-4349-912f-aa3f27949343"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"correlation matrix T\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     TagBox[
      RowBox[{"(", "\[NoBreak]", GridBox[{
         {"0", "0", "1"},
         {"0", "1", "0"},
         {"1", "0", "0"}
        },
        GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
            Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
             Offset[0.7]}, 
            Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
            Offset[0.2], {
             Offset[0.4]}, 
            Offset[0.2]}}], "\[NoBreak]", ")"}],
      Function[BoxForm`e$, 
       MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]},
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"singular values\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}]},
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"CHSH optimum S\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         SqrtBox["2"]}], "\"  \[TildeEqual]  \"", "2.8284271247461903`"},
      "RowDefault"]},
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"contextual fraction CF\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "+", 
         SqrtBox["2"]}], "\"  \[TildeEqual]  \"", "0.41421356237309515`"},
      "RowDefault"]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.93]}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.3}}, "Rows" -> {{1.1}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[804]=",ExpressionUUID->"a10f76ea-2fe0-4b2d-8175-b4933a2b88ad"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
S = 2\[Sqrt]2 and CF = \[Sqrt]2-1 exactly \[LongDash] the same two numbers \
cct_mbqc_hawking_certification.wl pins as its ground truth for an ideal \
carved pair. The mesh really does carry a genuine analogue-Hawking \
correlation, and the geometric lens really does certify it, live, from this \
notebook's own kernel.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e7985efd-96c8-4b31-adfd-ccf1bee07307"],

Cell["\<\
Carving the computation instead: Z-measuring the other six qubits leaves \
survivors {1,2,3}, the induced path of Stage 7, as a GHZ triple after one \
fixed local Clifford. That correction (H conjugates X into Z and Y into -Y) \
can be folded directly into which operator gets measured, rather than applied \
as a separate gate \[LongDash] so the circuit below performs the entire \
Anders-Browne OR(a,b) protocol as a single pass of genuine quantum \
measurements, with the byproduct correction left as classical post-processing \
of the outcomes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bdbf50b-d0a5-443d-9f49-2127df18b71c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
measNbr = Table[Select[nbrsOf[edges1, s], # > 3 &], {s, 1, 3}];
zMeasGates = Table[QuantumMeasurementOperator[{projPlus[PZ], projMinus[PZ]}, \
{q}], {q, 4, nQ}];
ghzSetting[t_] := If[t == 1, PY, PX];   (* GHZ-frame operator for qubit 2 *)
omg[t_] := If[t == 1, -PY, PZ];         (* H-conjugated operator for qubits \
1,3: H.X.H=Z, H.Y.H=-Y *)
orCircuit[a_, b_] := Module[{c = Mod[a + b, 2]},
  QuantumCircuitOperator[Join[gsGates, zMeasGates, {
     QuantumMeasurementOperator[{projPlus[omg[a]], projMinus[omg[a]]}, {1}],
     QuantumMeasurementOperator[{projPlus[ghzSetting[b]], \
projMinus[ghzSetting[b]]}, {2}],
     QuantumMeasurementOperator[{projPlus[omg[c]], projMinus[omg[c]]}, \
{3}]}]]];
Show[orCircuit[1, 0][\"Diagram\"], ImageSize -> 560]\
\>", "Input",
 CellOpen->False,
 CellLabel->
  "In[805]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a660b556-f277-4db3-8db5-f74ed94723e5"],

